// D1045's INTERIM — a `type` declared INSIDE A FUNCTION BODY is refused AT THE
// DECLARATION, and that refusal is the ONLY diagnostic the program gets.
//
// THIS IS THE SHADOWING SPELLING, the one face of the defect that was WRONG rather than
// merely refused. The local `P` parsed and was silently DROPPED (type names registered
// only from the module-level walk), so the annotation below resolved to the MODULE-scope
// `P` and the program was told `no field 'y' on P` — about a field the declaration two
// lines above it declares — plus a second complaint that the object literal sets `y`.
// Two diagnostics, neither of them naming the real problem.
//
// STRICTNESS IS THE PIN. The corpus requires every diagnostic to be declared by a
// directive and every directive to match one, so a second error here fails this file.
// That is the assertion: one message, at the declaration's own line.
//
// A body-scope `type` is RULED legal and lexically scoped (DECISIONS.md §"A `type`
